---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import refs from '../../../../../public/equipment/11-05/references.json';
import v from '../../../../../public/equipment/11-05/verification.json';
const a='/equipment/11-05/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Thorlabs PM100D · Console and numerical scale" subtitle="" description="Inspect a disconnected Thorlabs PM100D console and convert fixed example readings on a separate card." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment pm1105">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/11-05/">← Equipment 11-05</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#evidence">Sources &amp; checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">11-05 / Console-only exhibit and synthetic numerical scale</span><h2>Thorlabs PM100D · Console &amp; numerical scale</h2><p>Inspect the red-boot PM100D console with its screen off and no sensor. The separate card shows how fixed synthetic values look in W, mW, µW and dBm. It does not generate or measure light.</p></header>
<div class="dn-grid"><section class="dn-card"><h3>3D exhibit</h3>
<div class="dn-bar"><button data-view="whole">Whole exhibit</button><button data-view="front">Console face</button><button data-view="rear">Rear and stand</button><button data-view="side">Closed side</button><button data-view="chart">Numerical card</button><button id="camera-reset">Reset view</button></div>
<div class="dn-camera"><canvas id="pm100d-model" aria-label="Disconnected handheld PM100D console and independent numerical display"></canvas></div>
<p id="asset" class="dn-note" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="dn-note">Drag to orbit, pinch or scroll to zoom. On the detached card, the gold key cycles the fixed value and the pale key cycles its units. The actual-console buttons are static geometry.</p></section>
<section class="dn-card"><h3>Convert a known value</h3><div class="dn-bar"><label>Fixed value <select id="value"><option value="reference">1 mW</option><option value="tenth" selected>0.1 mW</option><option value="quarter">0.25 mW</option><option value="zero">Zero</option></select></label><label>Display unit <select id="unit"><option value="µW">µW</option><option value="mW">mW</option><option value="W">W</option><option value="dBm">dBm</option></select></label><button id="reset">Reset</button></div>
<canvas id="number-card" width="480" height="272" role="img" aria-label="Synthetic numerical conversion card with original power and converted output"></canvas>
<p class="dn-note" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Fixed 0.1 mW = 100 µW.</p>
<div class="dn-bar"><button id="json">Export reading JSON</button><a href={a+'example-reading.json'}>Example reading</a></div>
<p class="dn-note">The logarithmic reference is 1 mW, so 1 mW = 0 dBm and a tenfold reduction = −10 dBm. Zero is valid in linear units but has no finite dBm value; the JSON uses <code>null</code>. These are arithmetic examples, not limits, readings or calibration data for any detector.</p></section></div>
<section id="evidence"><h3>Sources and geometric verification</h3>
<div class="photo-pair">
<figure><img src={a+'reference-front.webp'} width="560" height="330" alt="Original 3D render of the red boot, dark key panel and inactive screen" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Original PM100D front render. From the <a href={refs.references[0].url}>Thorlabs 2023 manual, figs. 1–2</a>, the display is on the left, with a direction pad and three lower keys on the right.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={a+'reference-rear.webp'} width="560" height="330" alt="Original 3D render of the red-boot console rear, stowed stand and closed side details" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Original rear render of the same GLB. Manual figs. 3–4 identify the enclosure edge and support bracket. The modeled stand is stowed, and connector outlines have no function.</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<ul>{refs.references.map(r=><li><a href={r.url}>{r.title}</a>. {r.caption}</li>)}</ul>
<p>The red-boot console uses <b>183 × 109 × 40 mm</b> (long side × short side × thickness), with an <b>81.4 × 61.0 mm</b> active window, from the manufacturer's general-data table. The landscape rotation does not change those body dimensions. Corner radii, trim, rear support and key detail are estimated. No detector is selected or implied to be bundled; no laser, wavelength configuration, exposure, or sample workflow is modeled.</p>
<div class="dn-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{v.checks.map(c=><tr><th scope="row">{c.id}</th><td>{String(c.expected)} {c.unit}</td><td>{typeof c.actual==='number'?Number(c.actual.toFixed(8)):String(c.actual)} {c.unit}</td><td>{c.tolerance===0?'Exact':c.tolerance}</td><td>{c.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'build-model.py'} download>Editable model</a> · <a href={a+'pm100d-console.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'references.json'}>Reference notes</a> · <a href={a+'vr-station.json'}>VR action manifest</a> · <a href={a+'units.mjs'}>Unit conversion module</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification JSON</a>. No headset session tested.</p>
</section></article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/11-05/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
.pm1105{--dn-rule:color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 26%,transparent);max-width:1280px;margin:auto}.dn-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.08fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}.dn-card{min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--dn-rule);padding:.85rem;margin:.8rem 0}.dn-card h3{margin:.21rem 0 .6rem}.dn-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;margin:.53rem 0}.dn-bar,.dn-note,.dn-fig figcaption{font:.89rem/1.4 system-ui,sans-serif}
.pm1105 :is(button,select){font:inherit;padding:.4rem;background:var(--panel,Canvas);color:inherit;border:1px solid var(--dn-rule);border-radius:3px;min-height:38px;cursor:pointer}.pm1105 .primary{background:#34594f;color:#fff}.dn-camera{aspect-ratio:1.34;background:#263b40}.dn-camera canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}.pm1105 #number-card{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:492px;margin:.6rem 0}.dn-table{overflow:auto}.dn-table table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}.dn-table :is(td,th){border-bottom:1px solid var(--dn-rule);padding:.42rem;text-align:left}.dn-fig{margin:1rem 0;max-width:680px}.dn-fig img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.dn-fig figcaption{margin:.38rem 0}@media(max-width:850px){.dn-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
.pm1105 .photo-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.8rem;max-width:860px}.pm1105 .photo-pair figure{margin:0}.pm1105 .photo-pair img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.pm1105 .photo-pair figcaption{font:.86rem/1.4 system-ui,sans-serif;margin:.3rem 0}@media(max-width:600px){.pm1105 .photo-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
